{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba window_test.py | sed -n '1,414p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The whole-window measurement of the linking version (poc-v119) against old-2 (poc-v118, 2026-07-01..09-20), D699.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 window_test.py neither <scratch>      # $0: poc-v119 over the whole window, every link question answered \"neither\", every\n     4\t                                                #     other request from a copy of old-2's archive; the result must equal old-2\n     5\t  python3 window_test.py census-dry <scratch>   # $0: the census pass with every eligible pair answered \"reads\"; must stay old-2\n     6\t  python3 window_test.py probe-v2-dry <scratch> / probe-v2 <scratch> <draw> <ledger> <approved ceiling>   # version 2 of the\n     7\t                                                #     link question (WORDING-V2.md, D703): $0 dry pass, then a paid draw on D700's ledger\n     8\t  python3 window_test.py census <scratch> <draw> <ledger> <approved ceiling>   # paid (Jev only, at most $0.10, the ceiling Alex\n     9\t                                                #     names): the same pass with each link job sent to Jev and no link written, so the\n    10\t                                                #     replay stays old-2; one draw of the link decisions\n    11\t\n    12\tThe `neither` pass proves that poc-v119 without links is old-2 over all 1,884 articles (DESIGN.md table 3, first row, extended from the\n    13\tJuly prefix to the whole window), and lists every link question the version would ask: each opening of a number question with the\n    14\tnumber questions it was shown, the pairs eligible under D695, and the pairs not eligible with their reason.\n    15\t\"\"\"\n    16\timport json\n    17\timport math\n    18\timport shutil\n    19\timport sqlite3\n    20\timport sys\n    21\timport time\n    22\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    23\t\n    24\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n    25\tJULY = REPO / 'docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design'\n    26\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    27\tsys.path.insert(0, str(JULY))\n    28\tfrom hivemind import config, live_lock, model, replay, universe       # noqa: E402\n    29\tfrom hivemind.views import links                           # noqa: E402\n    30\timport july_test                                            # noqa: E402\n    31\timport rebuild_control                                      # noqa: E402\n    32\t\n    33\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    34\t\n    35\tOLD2 = july_test.OLD2\n    36\tITEMS = july_test.ITEMS\n    37\tV119 = july_test.V119\n    38\tUNIVERSE = july_test.UNIVERSE\n    39\tWINDOW = ('2026-07-01', '2026-09-20')\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef refused_rows():\n    43\t    \"\"\"old-2's answers its own run refused (the archive keeps them under the request's hash with a ':refused:' suffix, so no later\n    44\t    identical request is answered with them): {request hash: stored provider response}. A replay must meet each refusal again to\n    45\t    reach the stored retry.\"\"\"\n    46\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    47\t    return {sha.split(':refused:')[0]: json.loads(response) for sha, response in\n    48\t            stored.execute(\"select request_sha256, response_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:refused:%' order by call_id\")}\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef replay_window(folder, link_answer):\n    52\t    \"\"\"poc-v119 from an empty ledger over the whole window: link questions go to `link_answer`; every other request must be answered\n    53\t    from the copy of old-2's archive (an answer old-2's own run refused is given back once, so the check refuses it again); anything\n    54\t    else stops the pass. Returns the census: equality with old-2, every link job, every opening with its pairs.\"\"\"\n    55\t    if folder.exists():\n    56\t        raise SystemExit(f'{folder} exists: a pass starts from an empty folder')\n    57\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True)\n    58\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite')\n    59\t    views = folder / 'views.sqlite'\n    60\t    marker = sqlite3.connect(views)                 # marked harness-only before the first item: ordinary writers refuse it (D694 §0)\n    61\t    marker.execute('create table harness_only (name text, day text)')\n    62\t    marker.execute(\"insert into harness_only values ('window_test.py', '2026-11-21')\")\n    63\t    marker.commit()\n    64\t    marker.close()\n    65\t    held = live_lock.acquire(str(views))            # the store lock for the whole pass: no second writer\n    66\t    asked, refused_again = [], []\n    67\t    stored_refusals = refused_rows()\n    68\t\n    69\t    def transport(*args):\n    70\t        if len(args) == 1 and july_test.is_link_request(args[0]):\n    71\t            asked.append(sorted(args[0]['questions']))\n    72\t            return link_answer(args[0])\n    73\t        response = stored_refusals.pop(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1], None)\n    74\t        if response is not None:                   # old-2's own run refused this answer: give it back, so the check refuses it again\n    75\t            refused_again.append(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1][:12])\n    76\t            return response\n    77\t        (folder / 'missed-request.json').write_text(json.dumps(args[-1], ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n    78\t        raise july_test.Stop('a request other than a link question missed the archive')\n    79\t    started = time.time()\n    80\t    try:\n    81\t        totals = replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(views), archive=model.Archive(str(folder / 'archive.sqlite')),\n    82\t                            cfg=config.load(str(V119)), universe=universe.load(str(UNIVERSE)), from_day=WINDOW[0], until_day=WINDOW[1],\n    83\t                            transport=transport, log=lambda *a: None, only_objects={'NVDA'})\n    84\t    finally:\n    85\t        live_lock.release(held)\n    86\t    print('totals:', totals, 'seconds:', round(time.time() - started))\n    87\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    88\t    last_seq = conn.execute('select max(seq) from days_completed').fetchone()[0]\n    89\t    stored_last = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True).execute('select max(seq) from days_completed').fetchone()[0]\n    90\t    print('last completed seq', last_seq, 'old-2', stored_last)\n    91\t    equal = last_seq == stored_last and rebuild_control.compare(folder / 'views.sqlite', last_seq)\n    92\t    openings = []\n    93\t    for attempt, seq, status, record_json in conn.execute('select attempt_id, seq, status, record_json from link_selections order by id'):\n    94\t        record = json.loads(record_json)\n    95\t        if status == 'proposed' and record.get('pairs'):\n    96\t            openings.append({'attempt': attempt, 'seq': seq, 'pairs': record['pairs'], 'calls': record.get('calls', []),\n    97\t                             'proposed': record.get('proposed', []), 'corrections': record.get('corrections', [])})\n    98\t    census = {'equal to old-2': equal, 'link jobs asked': len(asked), 'questions in them': sum(len(a) for a in asked),\n    99\t              \"old-2's refused answers met again\": refused_again, 'left unmet': sorted(sha[:12] for sha in stored_refusals),\n   100\t              'link rows written': conn.execute(\"select count(*) from dependencies where kind='reads'\").fetchone()[0],\n   101\t              'openings with a pair shown': openings}\n   102\t    (folder / 'census.json').write_text(json.dumps(census, indent=1))\n   103\t    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in census.items() if k != 'openings with a pair shown'}, indent=1))\n   104\t    for opening in openings:\n   105\t        eligible = [p['thesis'] for p in opening['pairs'] if p.get('eligible')]\n   106\t        print(opening['seq'], 'eligible', eligible, 'not eligible', len(opening['pairs']) - len(eligible))\n   107\t    return census\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\tdef neither(scratch):\n   111\t    return replay_window(scratch / 'neither-v119', july_test.fake_jev(set()))['equal to old-2']\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\tCENSUS_CEILING = 0.10\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\tclass Everything:\n   118\t    def __contains__(self, item):\n   119\t        return True\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef without_links(run):\n   123\t    \"\"\"Run `run()` with the writer handed no proposed link (the census's only change to the product path).\"\"\"\n   124\t    from hivemind.views import writing\n   125\t    original_write = writing.write\n   126\t\n   127\t    def write_without_links(*args, **keywords):\n   128\t        keywords['proposed_links'] = None\n   129\t        return original_write(*args, **keywords)\n   130\t    writing.write = write_without_links\n   131\t    try:\n   132\t        return run()\n   133\t    finally:\n   134\t        writing.write = original_write\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\tdef complete(result):\n   138\t    \"\"\"A draw counts only when it asked every registered pair and finished each stage: the READS answers per opening are exactly the\n   139\t    eligible pairs of the `neither` pass, every READS answer that passed (a reading direction at 0.5 or more) has its SIGN answer, and\n   140\t    every Jev job was answered. Returns (complete, problems).\"\"\"\n   141\t    expected = {(o['seq'], p['thesis']) for o in json.loads((HERE / 'neither-census.json').read_text())['openings with a pair shown']\n   142\t                for p in o['pairs'] if p.get('eligible')}\n   143\t    problems, reads, signs = [], set(), set()\n   144\t    for opening in result['openings with a pair shown']:\n   145\t        for pair in opening['pairs']:\n   146\t            if 'reads' in pair:\n   147\t                reads.add((opening['seq'], pair['thesis']))\n   148\t                choice = pair['reads']\n   149\t                if choice != links.NEITHER and pair['probabilities'].get(choice, 0) >= links.THRESHOLD:\n   150\t                    signs.add((opening['seq'], pair['thesis']))\n   151\t        answered_signs = {(opening['seq'], p['thesis']) for p in opening['pairs'] if 'sign' in p}\n   152\t        missing = {s for s in signs if s[0] == opening['seq']} - answered_signs\n   153\t        if missing:\n   154\t            problems.append(f'seq {opening[\"seq\"]}: no SIGN answer for {sorted(missing)}')\n   155\t        problems += [f'seq {opening[\"seq\"]}: a job {c.get(\"stage\")} ended {c.get(\"status\")}' for c in opening['calls'] if c.get('status') != 'answered']\n   156\t    if reads != expected:\n   157\t        problems.append(f'READS pairs differ from the registered manifest: missing {sorted(expected - reads)}, extra {sorted(reads - expected)}')\n   158\t    return not problems, problems\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\tdef census_dry(scratch):\n   162\t    \"\"\"$0: the census pass with a fake Jev that answers every eligible pair \"the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE\", sign together (the\n   163\t    largest number of proposals); with the writer handed no link, the pass must still end equal to old-2 with no link row, and the\n   164\t    draw must be complete (every registered READS pair, a SIGN answer for each).\"\"\"\n   165\t    result = without_links(lambda: replay_window(scratch / 'census-dry', july_test.fake_jev(Everything())))\n   166\t    proposed = sum(len(o['proposed']) for o in result['openings with a pair shown'])\n   167\t    whole, problems = complete(result)\n   168\t    print('links proposed by the fake answers:', proposed, 'complete:', whole, problems)\n   169\t    return result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0 and proposed == 105 and whole\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\tdef census(scratch, draw, ledger_path, approved):\n   173\t    \"\"\"One draw of the link decisions over the window: each link job sent to Jev as poc-v119 builds it, through the comparison runs'\n   174\t    reservation ledger (`july_test.budget_module`: Jev reserved at its published 64K limit for each of its three attempts); the\n   175\t    writer is handed no proposed link, so no link row is written and every later request stays old-2's (the pass checks equality at the\n   176\t    end). The ledger is created beforehand with the ceiling Alex approved; each draw registers its launcher, so the stop gate stops\n   177\t    every draw when one dies. A draw is counted only when it is complete and the ledger never stopped.\"\"\"\n   178\t    budget = july_test.budget_module()\n   179\t    if not (isinstance(approved, float) and math.isfinite(approved) and 0 < approved <= CENSUS_CEILING):\n   180\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling must be a finite amount above 0 and at most ${CENSUS_CEILING}')\n   181\t    if not Path(ledger_path).exists():\n   182\t        raise SystemExit('the ledger does not exist: create it first (budget_replay.py --init-ledger L --ceiling <approved>)')\n   183\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   184\t    ceiling = ledger.read()['ceiling']\n   185\t    if not (isinstance(ceiling, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(ceiling) and ceiling == approved):\n   186\t        raise SystemExit(f'the ledger ceiling {ceiling!r} is not the approved ${approved}: refused')\n   187\t    label = f'census-{draw}'\n   188\t    lock_handle = open(Path(ledger_path).with_name(f'{label}.launcher.lock'), 'a+')\n   189\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher(label, lock_handle):\n   190\t        raise SystemExit(f'another launch of {label} is running')\n   191\t    budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   192\t    try:\n   193\t        return census_pass(scratch / label, draw, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger.read, 'paid')\n   194\t    finally:\n   195\t        ledger.remove_launcher(label)\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\tJULY_SEQ = 148\n   199\tJULY_HASHES = {'6dcb76643aea831174f8c0811f5f9329ebf5ac60f072a6be4f6992fac2e698a1',     # READS, v14's opening against v1, v2, v8, v9\n   200\t               'd118a387e9861b93b1d19c79dc9d46f18f78c06b8e7243aa33940f269c9d81a2'}     # SIGN, v9\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef census_pass(folder, draw, inner, ledger_state, transport_kind, stored=None):\n   204\t    \"\"\"One census draw into `folder`: the seq-148 jobs answered by this draw's July sample, every other link job by `inner`, the writer\n   205\t    handed no link. A link job at seq 148 whose request is not one of the two pinned July requests stops the pass before `inner`\n   206\t    (nothing is bought there). Writes `draw.json` with the transport kind ('paid' or 'dry'); the draw is counted only when it is\n   207\t    complete, reused both July answers, ended equal to old-2 with no link row, and the ledger neither stopped nor overran.\"\"\"\n   208\t    from hivemind.views import round as round_module\n   209\t    stored = july_answers(draw) if stored is None else stored\n   210\t    reused, current = [], {'seq': None}\n   211\t\n   212\t    def link_answer(request):\n   213\t        sha = model.request_identity(request)[1]\n   214\t        if sha in stored:                          # the July sample of this draw for the same request (seq 148): not bought again\n   215\t            reused.append(sha[:12])\n   216\t            return stored[sha]\n   217\t        if current['seq'] == JULY_SEQ:\n   218\t            raise july_test.Stop(f'a link job at seq {JULY_SEQ} is not one of the pinned July requests ({sha[:12]}): not sent')\n   219\t        return inner(request)\n   220\t    original_run = round_module.run\n   221\t\n   222\t    def run_noting_seq(conn, archive, cfg, uni, item, seq, *args, **keywords):\n   223\t        current['seq'] = seq\n   224\t        return original_run(conn, archive, cfg, uni, item, seq, *args, **keywords)\n   225\t    round_module.run = run_noting_seq\n   226\t    try:\n   227\t        result = without_links(lambda: replay_window(folder, link_answer))\n   228\t    finally:\n   229\t        round_module.run = original_run\n   230\t    state = ledger_state()\n   231\t    whole, problems = complete(result)\n   232\t    if sorted(reused) != sorted(sha[:12] for sha in stored):\n   233\t        whole, problems = False, problems + [f'July samples reused {reused}, expected {sorted(sha[:12] for sha in stored)}']\n   234\t    counted = result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0 and whole and not state.get('stopped') and not state.get('overrun')\n   235\t    (folder / 'draw.json').write_text(json.dumps({'draw': draw, 'transport': transport_kind, 'counted': counted, 'complete': whole, 'problems': problems,\n   236\t                                                  'equal to old-2': result['equal to old-2'], 'july samples reused': reused,\n   237\t                                                  'ledger': state}, indent=1))\n   238\t    print('ledger:', state, 'complete:', whole, problems, 'july reused:', reused)\n   239\t    return counted\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\tdef census_reuse_dry(scratch):\n   243\t    \"\"\"$0: a census draw whose bought jobs are answered \"neither\" by a fake Jev: the seq-148 jobs must be answered by draw 1's July\n   244\t    sample (both reused), the draw complete and counted, and the record must show v9 reads v14 proposed at seq 148.\"\"\"\n   245\t    counted = census_pass(scratch / 'census-reuse-dry', '1', july_test.fake_jev(set()), lambda: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False}, 'dry')\n   246\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{scratch / \"census-reuse-dry\" / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   247\t    proposed = [json.loads(r)['proposed'] for (r,) in conn.execute(\"select record_json from link_selections where status='proposed' and seq=148\")]\n   248\t    print('seq 148 proposed:', proposed)\n   249\t    return counted and proposed and len(proposed[0]) == 1\n   250\t\n   251\t\n   252\tJULY_DRAWS = {'1': 'linked-1', '2': 'linked-2', '3': 'linked-3'}\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\tdef july_answers(draw):\n   256\t    \"\"\"The July test's answers to the seq-148 link jobs (READS, call 8738; SIGN, call 8739) of the linked sequence paired with this\n   257\t    draw: {request hash: stored Jev response}. The census rebuilds the same READS request (sha 6dcb7664…); the SIGN request matches\n   258\t    when the READS answer passes the same pairs, which the reused answer guarantees.\"\"\"\n   259\t    if draw not in JULY_DRAWS:\n   260\t        raise SystemExit(f'draw must be one of {sorted(JULY_DRAWS)} (each reuses one July sequence\\'s seq-148 answers)')\n   261\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{REPO / \"poc/data/july-link-test-2026-11-21\" / JULY_DRAWS[draw] / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   262\t    return pinned({sha: json.loads(response) for sha, response in\n   263\t                   archive.execute('select request_sha256, response_json from model_calls where call_id in (8738, 8739)')})\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\tdef pinned(stored):\n   267\t    \"\"\"The July answers, refused unless they are exactly the two pinned requests (checked before anything is sent).\"\"\"\n   268\t    if set(stored) != JULY_HASHES:\n   269\t        raise SystemExit(f'the July answers are not the two pinned requests: {sorted(s[:12] for s in stored)}')\n   270\t    return stored\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\tdef reuse_refusals(scratch):\n   274\t    \"\"\"$0: (1) a July loader missing one pinned row is refused before anything runs; (2) a seq-148 link job whose request is not\n   275\t    pinned stops the pass before the inner transport (the pass is given draw 1's SIGN answer only, so the seq-148 READS job is\n   276\t    unpinned); the inner transport records every call it receives.\"\"\"\n   277\t    full = july_answers('1')\n   278\t    one = {sha: answer for sha, answer in full.items() if sha.startswith('d118')}\n   279\t    try:\n   280\t        pinned(one)\n   281\t        loader = 'NOT REFUSED'\n   282\t    except SystemExit as error:\n   283\t        loader = f'refused: {error}'\n   284\t    received = []\n   285\t\n   286\t    def recording(request):\n   287\t        received.append(sorted(request['questions']))\n   288\t        return july_test.fake_jev(set())(request)\n   289\t    try:\n   290\t        census_pass(scratch / 'reuse-refusal', '1', recording, lambda: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False}, 'dry', stored=one)\n   291\t        stop = 'NOT STOPPED'\n   292\t    except july_test.Stop as error:\n   293\t        stop = f'stopped: {error}'\n   294\t    except RuntimeError as error:                   # replay.run wraps a failed item's stop\n   295\t        stop = f'stopped: {error}'\n   296\t    at_148 = [q for q in received if 'reads__v9' in q]\n   297\t    print(json.dumps({'loader missing a pinned row': loader, 'unpinned seq-148 job': stop,\n   298\t                      'seq-148 READS job reached the inner transport': bool(at_148), 'inner calls before the stop': len(received)}, indent=1))\n   299\t    return loader.startswith('refused') and stop.startswith('stopped') and not at_148\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t\n   303\t# ---------- version 2 of the link question (WORDING-V2.md, D703): a harness-only probe ----------\n   304\t\n   305\tV2_TIE_BREAK = (\" When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no \"\n   306\t                \"guidance, consensus or reported figure for its period) is the one judged with the other's conclusion in view.\")\n   307\tV2_PERIODS = (\" or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a \"\n   308\t              \"retailer's sales this year and its sales growth next year);\")\n   309\tV2_BASE = \"; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth)\"\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\tdef wording_v2():\n   313\t    \"\"\"The version-2 READS and SIGN criteria: the current texts with the three changes of WORDING-V2.md §2 (each anchored on a unique\n   314\t    phrase of the current text, so a moved text fails loudly).\"\"\"\n   315\t    reads, sign = dict(links.READS), dict(links.SIGN)\n   316\t    reads[links.CANDIDATE_READS] = reads[links.CANDIDATE_READS] + V2_TIE_BREAK\n   317\t    anchor = \"for the same period and scope;\"\n   318\t    assert reads[links.NEITHER].count(anchor) == 1\n   319\t    reads[links.NEITHER] = reads[links.NEITHER].replace(anchor, \"for the same period and scope,\" + V2_PERIODS)\n   320\t    tail = \"a retailer's markdowns and its gross margin)\"\n   321\t    assert sign[links.OPPOSITE].endswith(tail)\n   322\t    sign[links.OPPOSITE] = sign[links.OPPOSITE][:-1] + V2_BASE\n   323\t    return reads, sign\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\tdef with_wording_v2(run):\n   327\t    reads, sign = wording_v2()\n   328\t    original = links.READS, links.SIGN\n   329\t    links.READS, links.SIGN = reads, sign\n   330\t    try:\n   331\t        return run()\n   332\t    finally:\n   333\t        links.READS, links.SIGN = original\n   334\t\n   335\t\n   336\tdef probe_pass(folder, draw, inner, ledger_state, transport_kind):\n   337\t    \"\"\"One version-2 draw into `folder`: every link job asked with the version-2 texts (none matches a July request, so all are sent to\n   338\t    `inner`), the writer handed no link. Every request must carry the version-2 texts (checked as it is sent). Writes `draw.json`; the\n   339\t    draw is counted only when it is complete, ended equal to old-2 with no link row, and the ledger neither stopped nor overran.\"\"\"\n   340\t    reads, sign = wording_v2()\n   341\t    carried = []\n   342\t\n   343\t    def link_answer(request):\n   344\t        texts = [q['criteria'] for q in request['questions'].values()]\n   345\t        expected = reads if next(iter(request['questions'])).startswith('reads__') else sign\n   346\t        if any(criteria != {k: v for k, v in expected.items() if k in criteria} for criteria in texts):\n   347\t            raise july_test.Stop('a link job does not carry the version-2 criteria: not sent')\n   348\t        carried.append(len(texts))\n   349\t        return inner(request)\n   350\t    result = with_wording_v2(lambda: without_links(lambda: replay_window(folder, link_answer)))\n   351\t    state = ledger_state()\n   352\t    whole, problems = complete(result)\n   353\t    counted = result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0 and whole and bool(carried) and not state.get('stopped') and not state.get('overrun')\n   354\t    (folder / 'draw.json').write_text(json.dumps({'draw': draw, 'wording': 'v2', 'transport': transport_kind, 'counted': counted,\n   355\t                                                  'complete': whole, 'problems': problems, 'equal to old-2': result['equal to old-2'],\n   356\t                                                  'jobs carrying version 2': len(carried), 'ledger': state}, indent=1))\n   357\t    print('ledger:', state, 'complete:', whole, problems, 'jobs carrying version 2:', len(carried))\n   358\t    return counted\n   359\t\n   360\t\n   361\tdef probe_v2_dry(scratch):\n   362\t    \"\"\"$0: the version-2 pass with every pair answered \"reads\", sign together: complete, equal to old-2, every job carrying the\n   363\t    version-2 texts, 105 proposals.\"\"\"\n   364\t    counted = probe_pass(scratch / 'probe-v2-dry', 'dry', july_test.fake_jev(Everything()), lambda: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False}, 'dry')\n   365\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{scratch / \"probe-v2-dry\" / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   366\t    proposed = sum(len(json.loads(r)['proposed']) for (r,) in conn.execute(\"select record_json from link_selections where status='proposed'\"))\n   367\t    print('proposals:', proposed)\n   368\t    return counted and proposed == 105\n   369\t\n   370\t\n   371\tdef probe_v2(scratch, draw, ledger_path, approved):\n   372\t    \"\"\"One paid version-2 draw on D700's ledger (the same checks as `census`: approved finite ceiling equal to the ledger's, launcher\n   373\t    registered, stop gate installed).\"\"\"\n   374\t    budget = july_test.budget_module()\n   375\t    if not (isinstance(approved, float) and math.isfinite(approved) and 0 < approved <= CENSUS_CEILING):\n   376\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling must be a finite amount above 0 and at most ${CENSUS_CEILING}')\n   377\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   378\t    ceiling = ledger.read()['ceiling']\n   379\t    if not (isinstance(ceiling, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(ceiling) and ceiling == approved):\n   380\t        raise SystemExit(f'the ledger ceiling {ceiling!r} is not the approved ${approved}: refused')\n   381\t    if draw not in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   382\t        raise SystemExit('draw must be 1, 2 or 3')\n   383\t    label = f'probe-v2-{draw}'\n   384\t    lock_handle = open(Path(ledger_path).with_name(f'{label}.launcher.lock'), 'a+')\n   385\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher(label, lock_handle):\n   386\t        raise SystemExit(f'another launch of {label} is running')\n   387\t    budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   388\t    try:\n   389\t        return probe_pass(scratch / label, draw, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger.read, 'paid')\n   390\t    finally:\n   391\t        ledger.remove_launcher(label)\n   392\t\n   393\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   394\t    command, scratch = sys.argv[1], Path(sys.argv[2])\n   395\t    if command == 'neither':\n   396\t        sys.exit(0 if neither(scratch) else 1)\n   397\t    if command == 'census-dry':\n   398\t        sys.exit(0 if census_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   399\t    if command == 'census-reuse-dry':\n   400\t        sys.exit(0 if census_reuse_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   401\t    if command == 'reuse-refusals':\n   402\t        sys.exit(0 if reuse_refusals(scratch) else 1)\n   403\t    if command == 'probe-v2-dry':\n   404\t        sys.exit(0 if probe_v2_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   405\t    if command == 'probe-v2':\n   406\t        sys.exit(0 if probe_v2(scratch, sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4]), float(sys.argv[5])) else 1)\n   407\t    if command == 'census':\n   408\t        sys.exit(0 if census(scratch, sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4]), float(sys.argv[5])) else 1)\n   409\t    raise SystemExit(f'unknown command {command}')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba read_census.py; nl -ba expected_links.py; nl -ba probe-v2-dry.log | tail -10; nl -ba probe-v2-mutant.log; nl -ba scorer-checks.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba read_census.py; nl -ba expected_links.py; nl -ba probe-v2-dry.log | tail -10; nl -ba probe-v2-mutant.log; nl -ba scorer-checks.log'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"Score the census draws against the registered reading (`expected-links.json`, written before any census answer was read).\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 read_census.py <census-1 folder> <census-2 folder> <census-3 folder> > census-pairs.md\n     4\t  python3 read_census.py --v2 <probe-v2-1> <probe-v2-2> <probe-v2-3> > probe-v2-pairs.md   # version 2 (WORDING-V2.md), its own\n     5\t                                                # registration (`expected-links-v2.json`: the census's classes plus F)\n     6\t\n     7\tThe scorer refuses unless it is given exactly three distinct draws (1, 2, 3), each with a `draw.json` that says it was a paid draw and was counted\n     8\t(complete, both July seq-148 answers reused, equal to old-2, no link row, the ledger never stopped or overran: `window_test.census`),\n     9\tand unless every registered pair has a READS answer in every draw.\n    10\t\n    11\tPer pair and draw: the READS answer (choice and probabilities), the SIGN answer when asked, and the decision the product takes (a link\n    12\tneeds a reading direction at 0.5 or more and a sign of together or opposite at 0.5 or more). Verdicts:\n    13\t  R pair (the known positive): right only when the registered direction is linked with the sign together (a higher total makes a\n    14\t    higher Data Center figure more likely); missed when no link is written; wrong for the opposite direction or the opposite sign;\n    15\t  W pair: wrong if linked, right if not;\n    16\t  F pair (version 2 only): wrong when linked in the forbidden direction with the forbidden sign; otherwise reported;\n    17\t  O pair: reported only.\n    18\tA margin (the winning READS probability minus the next) below 0.10 on a linked or a required pair is flagged as fragile.\n    19\tThe gate (DESIGN.md §3; WORDING-V2.md §3): no wrong link (W, or F for version 2) in any draw, and the known positive right in every\n    20\tdraw.\n    21\t\"\"\"\n    22\timport json\n    23\timport sqlite3\n    24\timport sys\n    25\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    26\t\n    27\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    28\tTHRESHOLD = 0.5\n    29\tREADS = {'candidate_reads_thesis', 'thesis_reads_candidate'}\n    30\tSIGNS = {'together', 'opposite'}\n    31\tREQUIRED_SIGN = 'together'\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tclass Refused(SystemExit):\n    35\t    pass\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef decisions(views_path):\n    39\t    \"\"\"{(seq, thesis): {'reads': choice, 'p': probabilities, 'sign': choice or None, 'sp': probabilities or None}}\"\"\"\n    40\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{views_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    41\t    out = {}\n    42\t    for seq, record_json in conn.execute(\"select seq, record_json from link_selections where status='proposed' order by id\"):\n    43\t        for pair in json.loads(record_json).get('pairs', []):\n    44\t            if 'thesis' not in pair:\n    45\t                continue\n    46\t            entry = out.setdefault((seq, pair['thesis']), {'reads': None, 'p': None, 'sign': None, 'sp': None})\n    47\t            if 'reads' in pair:\n    48\t                entry['reads'], entry['p'] = pair['reads'], pair['probabilities']\n    49\t            if 'sign' in pair:\n    50\t                entry['sign'], entry['sp'] = pair['sign'], pair['probabilities']\n    51\t    return out\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef linked(entry, new, thesis):\n    55\t    \"\"\"(direction '<reader> reads <read>', sign) the product writes, or (None, None).\"\"\"\n    56\t    if entry['reads'] not in READS or entry['p'][entry['reads']] < THRESHOLD:\n    57\t        return None, None\n    58\t    if entry['sign'] not in SIGNS or entry['sp'][entry['sign']] < THRESHOLD:\n    59\t        return None, None\n    60\t    direction = f'{new} reads {thesis}' if entry['reads'] == 'candidate_reads_thesis' else f'{thesis} reads {new}'\n    61\t    return direction, entry['sign']\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef margin(entry):\n    65\t    values = sorted(entry['p'].values(), reverse=True)\n    66\t    return round(values[0] - values[1], 2)\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef score(draws, expected):\n    70\t    \"\"\"draws: [(name, decisions)]. Returns (rows, summary); refuses when a registered pair has no READS answer in a draw.\"\"\"\n    71\t    rows, wrong, missed, right, fragile, positive = [], [], [], [], [], []\n    72\t    for key, reg in expected.items():\n    73\t        seq, thesis = int(key.split(':')[0]), key.split(':')[1]\n    74\t        cells = []\n    75\t        for name, answers in draws:\n    76\t            entry = answers.get((seq, thesis))\n    77\t            if entry is None or entry['p'] is None:\n    78\t                raise Refused(f'{name}: no READS answer for the registered pair {key}')\n    79\t            direction, sign = linked(entry, reg['new'], thesis)\n    80\t            m = margin(entry)\n    81\t            short = {'candidate_reads_thesis': 'new→', 'thesis_reads_candidate': '←new', 'neither': 'none'}[entry['reads']]\n    82\t            cell = f\"{short} {entry['p'][entry['reads']]:.2f} (m {m:.2f})\" + (f\"; {entry['sign']} {entry['sp'][entry['sign']]:.2f}\" if entry['sign'] else '')\n    83\t            if reg['class'] == 'R':\n    84\t                if direction is None:\n    85\t                    verdict = 'missed'\n    86\t                elif direction == reg['direction'] and sign == REQUIRED_SIGN:\n    87\t                    verdict = 'right'\n    88\t                else:\n    89\t                    verdict = 'WRONG'\n    90\t                positive.append(verdict == 'right')\n    91\t            elif reg['class'] == 'W':\n    92\t                verdict = 'WRONG' if direction else 'right'\n    93\t            elif reg['class'] == 'F':\n    94\t                verdict = 'WRONG' if (direction, sign) == tuple(reg['forbidden']) else (f'linked: {direction} ({sign})' if direction else 'no link')\n    95\t            else:\n    96\t                verdict = f'linked: {direction} ({sign})' if direction else 'no link'\n    97\t            if verdict == 'WRONG':\n    98\t                wrong.append((name, key, direction, sign))\n    99\t            elif verdict == 'missed':\n   100\t                missed.append((name, key))\n   101\t            elif verdict == 'right' and reg['class'] == 'R':\n   102\t                right.append((name, key))\n   103\t            if (direction or reg['class'] == 'R') and m < 0.10:\n   104\t                fragile.append((name, key, m))\n   105\t            cells.append(f'{cell} → {verdict}')\n   106\t        rows.append((seq, reg, thesis, cells))\n   107\t    gate = not wrong and bool(positive) and all(positive)\n   108\t    return rows, {'right': right, 'missed': missed, 'wrong': wrong, 'fragile': fragile, 'gate': gate}\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef counted_draws(folders, wording=None):\n   112\t    if len(folders) != 3:\n   113\t        raise Refused(f'three census draws are required, got {len(folders)}')\n   114\t    seen = []\n   115\t    for folder in folders:\n   116\t        record_path = Path(folder) / 'draw.json'\n   117\t        if not record_path.exists():\n   118\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: no draw.json (not a census draw)')\n   119\t        record = json.loads(record_path.read_text())\n   120\t        if record.get('transport') != 'paid':\n   121\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: not a paid draw (transport {record.get(\"transport\")!r})')\n   122\t        if record.get('wording') != wording:\n   123\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: wording {record.get(\"wording\")!r}, expected {wording!r}')\n   124\t        if not record.get('counted'):\n   125\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: the draw was not counted: {record.get(\"problems\")}')\n   126\t        seen.append(record['draw'])\n   127\t    if sorted(seen) != ['1', '2', '3']:\n   128\t        raise Refused(f'the draws must be 1, 2 and 3, got {seen}')\n   129\t    return [(Path(f).name, decisions(Path(f) / 'views.sqlite')) for f in folders]\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\tdef main(folders):\n   133\t    wording = None\n   134\t    if folders and folders[0] == '--v2':\n   135\t        wording, folders = 'v2', folders[1:]\n   136\t    expected = json.loads((HERE / ('expected-links-v2.json' if wording == 'v2' else 'expected-links.json')).read_text())\n   137\t    draws = counted_draws(folders, wording)\n   138\t    rows, summary = score(draws, expected)\n   139\t    print('# Census of the link decisions over the window, scored against the registered reading\\n')\n   140\t    print('| seq | new | shown | class | registered | ' + ' | '.join(name for name, _ in draws) + ' |')\n   141\t    print('|---|---|---|---|---|' + '---|' * len(draws))\n   142\t    for seq, reg, thesis, cells in rows:\n   143\t        print(f\"| {seq} | {reg['new']} | {thesis} | {reg['class']} | {reg['direction'] or ''} | \" + ' | '.join(cells) + ' |')\n   144\t    print(f'\\nDraws: 3 (the seq-148 jobs of each answered by its paired July sample).')\n   145\t    print(f\"Known positive right: {len(summary['right'])}; missed: {len(summary['missed'])} {summary['missed']}\")\n   146\t    print(f\"Wrong links: {len(summary['wrong'])} {summary['wrong']}\")\n   147\t    print(f\"Fragile (margin below 0.10 on a linked or required pair): {len(summary['fragile'])} {summary['fragile']}\")\n   148\t    print(f\"\\nGate (no wrong link in any draw; the known positive right in every draw): {'PASS' if summary['gate'] else 'FAIL'}\")\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   152\t    main(sys.argv[1:])\n     1\t\"\"\"The registered reading of every eligible pair of the census, written before any census answer is read (council R round 13): each\n     2\tof the 105 pairs of `neither-census.json` gets one class.\n     3\t\n     4\t  R  the required link, with its direction and sign: the known positive only (round 14), Data Center revenue reading total revenue\n     5\t     (D537's clear case; the READS criterion's own first example, a product line read against the company's total). Missing it is a\n     6\t     miss; the opposite direction or the opposite sign is a wrong link.\n     7\t  W  any link is wrong: neither answer bounds or drives the other (the criterion's \"neither\" class) and the material each was shown\n     8\t     names no connection: a financing or commitment amount against a revenue, growth or margin question (supply commitments, and credit\n     9\t     support against revenue, excepted below), and two financing amounts of different kinds.\n    10\t  O  open: defensible either way under the criterion as written (overlapping scopes; growth against the amount it is computed from;\n    11\t     another period of the same quantity; supply commitments against revenue or margin; gross margin against revenue). Reported, not\n    12\t     scored.\n    13\t\n    14\tThe seq-148 pairs were seen before this registration (the July test's answers): disclosed with every score.\n    15\t\n    16\t  python3 expected_links.py > expected-links.md\n    17\t\"\"\"\n    18\timport json\n    19\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    20\t\n    21\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    22\tREQUIRED = {('v9', 'v14'): 'Data Center revenue read against total revenue: D537\\'s clear case, the known positive'}\n    23\tFINANCING = {'v1', 'v2', 'v15', 'v29', 'v32', 'v36'}\n    24\tBASE_EFFECT_READ = {'v8', 'v9', 'v14', 'v16'}      # FY2027 revenue amounts; v17 is FY2028 total revenue growth\n    25\tREVENUE = {'v8', 'v9', 'v14', 'v16', 'v17', 'v21', 'v35'}\n    26\tMARGIN = {'v28', 'v33'}\n    27\tCREDIT = {'v1', 'v2'}\n    28\tOPEN_FINANCING = {frozenset({'v1', 'v2'}): 'AI-cloud credit support sits inside all customer and cloud-provider credit support; either may read the other',\n    29\t                  frozenset({'v15', 'v32'}): 'a licence payment commitment may sit inside supply commitments',\n    30\t                  frozenset({'v29', 'v36'}): 'a convertible-bond investment may or may not count as an equity investment commitment',\n    31\t                  frozenset({'v2', 'v15'}): 'the shown repurchase of unsold GPU capacity may sit inside supply commitments (round 15)'}\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tdef classify(a, b):\n    35\t    \"\"\"(class, direction or None, reason) for the unordered pair a, b, from the scopes and the evidence each was shown with (round 14:\n    36\t    only the known positive is required; a W pair is one whose shown material names no connection).\"\"\"\n    37\t    for (reader, read), reason in REQUIRED.items():\n    38\t        if {a, b} == {reader, read}:\n    39\t            return 'R', f'{reader} reads {read}', reason\n    40\t    pair = frozenset({a, b})\n    41\t    if pair in OPEN_FINANCING:\n    42\t        return 'O', None, OPEN_FINANCING[pair]\n    43\t    if 'v15' in pair and pair & (REVENUE | MARGIN):\n    44\t        return 'O', None, 'supply commitments, shown as \"tying its fortunes to hyperscaler order books\", against revenue or margin'\n    45\t    if pair & CREDIT and pair & (REVENUE | MARGIN):\n    46\t        return 'O', None, 'the credit-support evidence shown says NVIDIA earns product revenue and a share of cloud revenue on the supported capacity and may buy back unsold capacity (revenue mix and cost paths into margin, round 15)'\n    47\t    if pair <= FINANCING:\n    48\t        return 'W', None, 'two financing amounts of different kinds; the shown material names no connection'\n    49\t    if pair & FINANCING and pair & (REVENUE | MARGIN):\n    50\t        return 'W', None, 'a financing amount against a revenue, growth or margin question; the shown material names no connection'\n    51\t    return 'O', None, 'part and whole far apart, overlapping scopes, growth against its amount, another period, or margin against revenue'\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef main():\n    55\t    census = json.loads((HERE / 'neither-census.json').read_text())\n    56\t    rows, counts = [], {'R': 0, 'W': 0, 'O': 0}\n    57\t    for opening in census['openings with a pair shown']:\n    58\t        for pair in opening['pairs']:\n    59\t            if not pair.get('eligible'):\n    60\t                continue\n    61\t            rows.append((opening['seq'], pair['thesis']))\n    62\t    import sqlite3\n    63\t    stored = sqlite3.connect('file:' + str(HERE.parents[2] / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite') + '?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    64\t    new_at = {seq: stored.execute('select view_id from views where created_seq=? and view_id in (select view_id from view_keys)', (seq,)).fetchone()[0]\n    65\t              for seq, _ in rows}\n    66\t    out = {}\n    67\t    print('# Registered reading of the census pairs (written before any census answer; `expected_links.py`)\\n')\n    68\t    print('| seq | new | shown | class | required direction | reason |')\n    69\t    print('|---|---|---|---|---|---|')\n    70\t    for seq, thesis in rows:\n    71\t        kind, direction, reason = classify(new_at[seq], thesis)\n    72\t        counts[kind] += 1\n    73\t        out[f'{seq}:{thesis}'] = {'new': new_at[seq], 'shown': thesis, 'class': kind, 'direction': direction}\n    74\t        print(f'| {seq} | {new_at[seq]} | {thesis} | {kind} | {direction or \"\"} | {reason} |')\n    75\t    print(f'\\nPairs: {len(rows)}; R {counts[\"R\"]}, W {counts[\"W\"]}, O {counts[\"O\"]}. The seq-148 pairs were seen before this registration.')\n    76\t    (HERE / 'expected-links.json').write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1))\n    77\t    # version 2's registration (WORDING-V2.md §3, written before its probe's answers): the census's classes plus F, the base-effect\n    78\t    # sign council R round 17 named: a growth rate reading an earlier period's revenue amount with the sign together\n    79\t    v2 = json.loads(json.dumps(out))\n    80\t    for key, entry in v2.items():\n    81\t        if entry['new'] == 'v17' and entry['shown'] in BASE_EFFECT_READ:\n    82\t            entry.update({'class': 'F', 'direction': None, 'forbidden': ('v17 reads ' + entry['shown'], 'together')})\n    83\t    (HERE / 'expected-links-v2.json').write_text(json.dumps(v2, indent=1))\n    84\t    print(f\"\\nVersion 2 adds F (forbidden: v17 reads an FY2027 revenue amount with the sign together): {sorted(k for k, e in v2.items() if e['class'] == 'F')}\")\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    88\t    main()\n    58\t1296 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    59\t1394 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    60\t1543 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    61\t1664 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    62\t1677 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    63\t1828 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    64\t1874 eligible [] not eligible 1\n    65\tledger: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False} complete: True [] jobs carrying version 2: 28\n    66\tproposals: 105\n    67\texit 0\n     1\tmutant (texts not patched) caught: RuntimeError ins resumable: linking: link question failed: Stop: a link job does not carry the version-2 criteria: not sent | inner calls: 0\n     1\tregistration: 1 R, 38 W, 66 O\n     2\tno draws: refused: three census draws are required, got 0\n     3\tthree folders without draw.json: refused: 0054109/scratchpad/window/census-dry: no draw.json (not a census draw)\n     4\tthe dry draw x3: refused: /scratchpad/window/census-reuse-dry: not a paid draw (transport 'dry')\n     5\tfake \"reads\" answers everywhere: wrong 114 known positive right 3 gate False\n     6\ta missing READS answer: refused: dry: no READS answer for the registered pair 1262:v1\n     7\tcontrol (only the known positive, together): gate True right 3\n     8\tmutant (known positive with sign opposite): gate False\n     9\tmutant (known positive reversed): gate False\n    10\tcensus draws under --v2: s-2026-11-21/census-1: wording None, expected 'v2'\n    11\tcensus answers scored on the v2 registration (positive control for F): wrong [('c1', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'together'), ('c2', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'together'), ('c3', '321:v16', 'v17 reads v16', 'together')] gate False\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba codex-r17.md; rg -n 'D260 ·' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '6457,6475p'; rg -n 'another period|Reads|period' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | head -25; rg -n '\"'^## (5|6|7)|Never grow|prompt audit'\"' ../../../AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba codex-r17.md; rg -n 'D260 ·' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '6457,6475p'; rg -n 'another period|Reads|period' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | head -25; rg -n '\"'^## (5|6|7)|Never grow|prompt audit'\"' ../../../AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t**PROBE A SHARPENED CRITERION FIRST.** The registered census PASS is sound. The reason to pause is a link the gate left open: all three draws told FY2028 revenue growth to read FY2027 CPU revenue with a positive sign, even though a higher prior-year base lowers growth if FY2028 revenue is held fixed. The shown evidence supplies no next-year CPU forecast to support the positive sign. [Census result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md:16) · [SIGN criterion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:32)\n     2\t\n     3\t## 1. The registered PASS holds\n     4\t\n     5\tI regenerated and read all 105 pairs across all three draws. I checked the recorded READS and SIGN choices and probabilities against their archived responses, reran the completeness check on each draw, and matched both reused responses to the corresponding July archive. All three draws count. The known positive is right **3 of 3**, none of the **114 W decisions** links, and the stores contain **zero committed links**. The ledger’s 52 Jev entries reconcile to **$0.02655387**, with no refusal or overrun. The result establishes a pass on the registered R and W cases. The positive at seq 148 is still the three July samples. [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:65) · [Completeness check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:135) · [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json:2)\n     6\t\n     7\tOne reporting correction: `CENSUS-RESULT.md` and `census-result.md` resolve to the same summary on this checkout. Give the regenerated pair table a distinct filename, and call the 7, 8 and 5 links **proposals**. [Summary’s table reference](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md:3) · [Scorer’s pair-table output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:124)\n     8\t\n     9\t## 2. Which links could hurt the reader\n    10\t\n    11\tBoth directions occur, and `v21–v9` is the only pair that flips direction. Four of the eight pairs vary in presence or direction. The scores support that narrower claim. They do not establish four near-even odds of flipping on a future run. [Observed links and margins](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md:16) · [Claude’s read](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/claude-r17.md:3)\n    12\t\n    13\t| Pair | Analyst read of the supplied material |\n    14\t|---|---|\n    15\t| `v9 reads v14` | Useful. The company total gives the segment a meaningful ceiling and a company-wide estimate it can translate with an explicit mix assumption. This is D537’s case. |\n    16\t| `v2 reads v1` | Defensible. AI-cloud credit support can inform the broader commitments estimate. The reader must account for overlap with guarantees and backstops before adding amounts. |\n    17\t| `v16 reads v14` | Weak. About $20B in CPU sales sits far below the $393B company estimate. The total is a ceiling, but the shown material gives little reason for it to move the likely CPU answer. |\n    18\t| `v17 reads v16` | The clearest risk. To the extent FY2027 CPU lifts the company’s FY2027 base, it pushes FY2028 percentage growth down at fixed FY2028 sales. A positive effect needs a next-year sales mechanism the request does not show. |\n    19\t| `v21 reads v16` | Defensible. FY2027 CPU sales contribute to the FY2027 numerator. The prior-year company total is still needed to translate the contribution into growth. |\n    20\t| `v21 reads v9` / `v9 reads v21` | Data Center can inform company growth because it accounted for 92% of the reported quarter. The reverse can help only if the reader converts the growth rate with the right prior-year base and reconciles it with the total forecast it already reads. Otherwise it risks counting two estimates of the same company-wide quantity as independent support. |\n    21\t| `v35 reads v14` | Defensible. The previous year’s company total is the base for a next-year level forecast built from growth. |\n    22\t| `v35 reads v9` | Weak and potentially misleading. The request shows a prior-year segment amount and next-year company estimates, with no segment carry-forward calculation. In draw 2 the reader already receives the prior-year company total that contains the segment. |\n    23\t\n    24\tThese are assessments of the inputs. The census bought no judgements, so it cannot show that any reader actually made a worse forecast. [Archived requests](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/census-1/archive.sqlite) · [READS and SIGN criteria](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:22) · [D537](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6457)\n    25\t\n    26\t## 3. The cheaper decision\n    27\t\n    28\tThe roughly **$7 estimated** comparison would tell Alex whether the **current mixture** improves judgements on old-2’s trajectory. A pass could make that version a replacement candidate. A failure could reveal harm, but would leave open whether clearer link selection would have preserved the benefit. [Paid-run estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md:39) · [D699](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10505)\n    29\t\n    30\tA cents-scale probe can first test whether requiring a clear link across periods, including how the prior-year base affects a growth rate, removes the unsupported positive sign while preserving the D537 link and the 38 negative pairs. I would avoid a blanket ban on whole-to-part reading: the credit-support example shows why a component can legitimately inform an aggregate. If the sharpened wording retains the useful links and removes the unsupported ones, take that version to Alex for the judgement design. If it loses the known positive or adds wrong links, retain the current wording as the candidate and bring its measured risks to the paid-design review. The probe would select what to test next. Its result would leave the judgement-quality question open. [READS criterion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:22) · [AGENTS §7.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:346)\n    31\t\n    32\t## 4. Reusing the census draws\n    33\t\n    34\t**Yes for these three recorded graphs, subject to a $0 replay check in the paid harness.** Ordinary READS uses the opening candidate and the shown question’s text, ladder and evidence. SIGN also uses the accepted READS direction, which replays with the paired answer. Writing a link adds the dependency and can queue a reader for judgement. That queue can change later **judgement** requests and propagate along the graph. It does not enter the matcher text, and `reads` rows are excluded from filing parents. [Request construction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:229) · [SIGN construction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:263) · [Writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:153) · [Filing parents](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:256) · [Judgement queue](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:327)\n    35\t\n    36\tThe exception is real: the chooser checks existing stored links, and a cycle can create a new correction request and possibly a new SIGN request. I ran the production cycle check in memory, adding each draw’s proposals in article order. **None of the three graphs triggered a correction.** Before buying judgements, have the actual linked harness commit the paired proposals at $0, verify each matcher request hash and the committed graph, and stop on any new matcher request. [Stored-graph check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:141) · [Correction requests](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:285) · [Archive lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:87)\n    37\t\n    38\t**PROBE A SHARPENED CRITERION FIRST**3049:## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n  6457\t## D537 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency-selection census has one clear case and negative controls; before any send, the edge's effect on filing and judging is proved on stored data (council consensus, reflection round 28)\n  6458\t\n  6459\t- **The census** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md`): over the fifteen\n  6460\t  questions the old system opened in the stored unseeded fresh week, 97 pairs on which a dependency could have been chosen (each\n  6461\t  new question against the questions it was compared with and its same-article siblings). Claude's own read written first, then\n  6462\t  two blind readers of different model families (the same mark on 68 of 97; both mark \"the new question would want the earlier\n  6463\t  one's conclusion\" on 11, three of them strong). One clear case: data-center revenue FY2027 against total revenue FY2027 (the\n  6464\t  matching engine recorded \"part of\", 1.00): the total's conclusion carried the year's consensus ($406.05 billion from 09-23,\n  6465\t  about $412 billion from 09-25) and the $108 billion guidance (from 09-26), none of them anywhere in the data-center question's\n  6466\t  seven requests; its last answer names the gap and adds a step of its own. Negative controls: the Hugging Face commitments\n  6467\t  question (\"none\" in all three readings); a weakly granted pair whose line would carry a judge's own assumed numbers. The\n  6468\t  strongest driver relations of the week (Rubin shipping against the revenue questions) run from a later question to an earlier\n  6469\t  one and cannot be chosen at creation (D191 point 2, decided, unbuilt).\n  6470\t- **The council's corrections:** the $96.2 billion quarter was already in all seven requests (not a figure the line would\n  6471\t  supply); the one \"same question\" pair is one unordered pair; the line would not by itself make the answer supported.\n  6472\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the pair is a positive lead for the decided dependency-selection slice (D368 item 2), not a\n  6473\t  validation of it. Before the council reviews any six-call send on it: a bounded proof on stored data of what the edge would do\n  6474\t  to filing and to judging (a statement linked to both questions, the direction, ordering, cycle rejection, what the judge's\n  6475\t  request would contain, the unrelated pair as a negative case), with no frozen file changed. Stop, and return the conflict to\n76: \"neither\": \"neither answer bounds or drives the other: unrelated quantities (a retailer's gross margin and its store openings in another country), or the same quantity for the same period and scope; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\"\n89:components), all number questions of the kind D695 admits; none names a company. Same-quantity-same-period is excluded because such a pair is one question (D248); another period of the\n211:point and the forecast); D248 (same quantity and period is one question); PRD 06 (cycles corrected, then normal failure); D354, D359\n168:## 5. Verification\n194:## 6. Writing prompts\n200:- **The prompt audit runs after every measurement and before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`). The whole\n220:- **Never grow a prompt to fix quality.** Read the whole request (system, schema, payload) as the model reads it, and list every\n237:## 7. Measuring and iterating\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba window_test.py | sed -n '303,420p'; nl -ba read_census.py | sed -n '20,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba window_test.py | sed -n '303,420p'; nl -ba read_census.py | sed -n '20,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"   303\t# ---------- version 2 of the link question (WORDING-V2.md, D703): a harness-only probe ----------\n   304\t\n   305\tV2_TIE_BREAK = (\" When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no \"\n   306\t                \"guidance, consensus or reported figure for its period) is the one judged with the other's conclusion in view.\")\n   307\tV2_PERIODS = (\" or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a \"\n   308\t              \"retailer's sales this year and its sales growth next year);\")\n   309\tV2_BASE = \"; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth)\"\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\tdef wording_v2():\n   313\t    \"\"\"The version-2 READS and SIGN criteria: the current texts with the three changes of WORDING-V2.md §2 (each anchored on a unique\n   314\t    phrase of the current text, so a moved text fails loudly).\"\"\"\n   315\t    reads, sign = dict(links.READS), dict(links.SIGN)\n   316\t    reads[links.CANDIDATE_READS] = reads[links.CANDIDATE_READS] + V2_TIE_BREAK\n   317\t    anchor = \"for the same period and scope;\"\n   318\t    assert reads[links.NEITHER].count(anchor) == 1\n   319\t    reads[links.NEITHER] = reads[links.NEITHER].replace(anchor, \"for the same period and scope,\" + V2_PERIODS)\n   320\t    tail = \"a retailer's markdowns and its gross margin)\"\n   321\t    assert sign[links.OPPOSITE].endswith(tail)\n   322\t    sign[links.OPPOSITE] = sign[links.OPPOSITE][:-1] + V2_BASE\n   323\t    return reads, sign\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\tdef with_wording_v2(run):\n   327\t    reads, sign = wording_v2()\n   328\t    original = links.READS, links.SIGN\n   329\t    links.READS, links.SIGN = reads, sign\n   330\t    try:\n   331\t        return run()\n   332\t    finally:\n   333\t        links.READS, links.SIGN = original\n   334\t\n   335\t\n   336\tdef probe_pass(folder, draw, inner, ledger_state, transport_kind):\n   337\t    \"\"\"One version-2 draw into `folder`: every link job asked with the version-2 texts (none matches a July request, so all are sent to\n   338\t    `inner`), the writer handed no link. Every request must carry the version-2 texts (checked as it is sent). Writes `draw.json`; the\n   339\t    draw is counted only when it is complete, ended equal to old-2 with no link row, and the ledger neither stopped nor overran.\"\"\"\n   340\t    reads, sign = wording_v2()\n   341\t    carried = []\n   342\t\n   343\t    def link_answer(request):\n   344\t        texts = [q['criteria'] for q in request['questions'].values()]\n   345\t        expected = reads if next(iter(request['questions'])).startswith('reads__') else sign\n   346\t        if any(criteria != {k: v for k, v in expected.items() if k in criteria} for criteria in texts):\n   347\t            raise july_test.Stop('a link job does not carry the version-2 criteria: not sent')\n   348\t        carried.append(len(texts))\n   349\t        return inner(request)\n   350\t    result = with_wording_v2(lambda: without_links(lambda: replay_window(folder, link_answer)))\n   351\t    state = ledger_state()\n   352\t    whole, problems = complete(result)\n   353\t    counted = result['equal to old-2'] and result['link rows written'] == 0 and whole and bool(carried) and not state.get('stopped') and not state.get('overrun')\n   354\t    (folder / 'draw.json').write_text(json.dumps({'draw': draw, 'wording': 'v2', 'transport': transport_kind, 'counted': counted,\n   355\t                                                  'complete': whole, 'problems': problems, 'equal to old-2': result['equal to old-2'],\n   356\t                                                  'jobs carrying version 2': len(carried), 'ledger': state}, indent=1))\n   357\t    print('ledger:', state, 'complete:', whole, problems, 'jobs carrying version 2:', len(carried))\n   358\t    return counted\n   359\t\n   360\t\n   361\tdef probe_v2_dry(scratch):\n   362\t    \"\"\"$0: the version-2 pass with every pair answered \"reads\", sign together: complete, equal to old-2, every job carrying the\n   363\t    version-2 texts, 105 proposals.\"\"\"\n   364\t    counted = probe_pass(scratch / 'probe-v2-dry', 'dry', july_test.fake_jev(Everything()), lambda: {'stopped': False, 'overrun': False}, 'dry')\n   365\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{scratch / \"probe-v2-dry\" / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   366\t    proposed = sum(len(json.loads(r)['proposed']) for (r,) in conn.execute(\"select record_json from link_selections where status='proposed'\"))\n   367\t    print('proposals:', proposed)\n   368\t    return counted and proposed == 105\n   369\t\n   370\t\n   371\tdef probe_v2(scratch, draw, ledger_path, approved):\n   372\t    \"\"\"One paid version-2 draw on D700's ledger (the same checks as `census`: approved finite ceiling equal to the ledger's, launcher\n   373\t    registered, stop gate installed).\"\"\"\n   374\t    budget = july_test.budget_module()\n   375\t    if not (isinstance(approved, float) and math.isfinite(approved) and 0 < approved <= CENSUS_CEILING):\n   376\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling must be a finite amount above 0 and at most ${CENSUS_CEILING}')\n   377\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   378\t    ceiling = ledger.read()['ceiling']\n   379\t    if not (isinstance(ceiling, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(ceiling) and ceiling == approved):\n   380\t        raise SystemExit(f'the ledger ceiling {ceiling!r} is not the approved ${approved}: refused')\n   381\t    if draw not in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   382\t        raise SystemExit('draw must be 1, 2 or 3')\n   383\t    label = f'probe-v2-{draw}'\n   384\t    lock_handle = open(Path(ledger_path).with_name(f'{label}.launcher.lock'), 'a+')\n   385\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher(label, lock_handle):\n   386\t        raise SystemExit(f'another launch of {label} is running')\n   387\t    budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   388\t    try:\n   389\t        return probe_pass(scratch / label, draw, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger.read, 'paid')\n   390\t    finally:\n   391\t        ledger.remove_launcher(label)\n   392\t\n   393\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   394\t    command, scratch = sys.argv[1], Path(sys.argv[2])\n   395\t    if command == 'neither':\n   396\t        sys.exit(0 if neither(scratch) else 1)\n   397\t    if command == 'census-dry':\n   398\t        sys.exit(0 if census_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   399\t    if command == 'census-reuse-dry':\n   400\t        sys.exit(0 if census_reuse_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   401\t    if command == 'reuse-refusals':\n   402\t        sys.exit(0 if reuse_refusals(scratch) else 1)\n   403\t    if command == 'probe-v2-dry':\n   404\t        sys.exit(0 if probe_v2_dry(scratch) else 1)\n   405\t    if command == 'probe-v2':\n   406\t        sys.exit(0 if probe_v2(scratch, sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4]), float(sys.argv[5])) else 1)\n   407\t    if command == 'census':\n   408\t        sys.exit(0 if census(scratch, sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4]), float(sys.argv[5])) else 1)\n   409\t    raise SystemExit(f'unknown command {command}')\n    20\tdraw.\n    21\t\"\"\"\n    22\timport json\n    23\timport sqlite3\n    24\timport sys\n    25\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    26\t\n    27\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    28\tTHRESHOLD = 0.5\n    29\tREADS = {'candidate_reads_thesis', 'thesis_reads_candidate'}\n    30\tSIGNS = {'together', 'opposite'}\n    31\tREQUIRED_SIGN = 'together'\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tclass Refused(SystemExit):\n    35\t    pass\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef decisions(views_path):\n    39\t    \"\"\"{(seq, thesis): {'reads': choice, 'p': probabilities, 'sign': choice or None, 'sp': probabilities or None}}\"\"\"\n    40\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{views_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    41\t    out = {}\n    42\t    for seq, record_json in conn.execute(\"select seq, record_json from link_selections where status='proposed' order by id\"):\n    43\t        for pair in json.loads(record_json).get('pairs', []):\n    44\t            if 'thesis' not in pair:\n    45\t                continue\n    46\t            entry = out.setdefault((seq, pair['thesis']), {'reads': None, 'p': None, 'sign': None, 'sp': None})\n    47\t            if 'reads' in pair:\n    48\t                entry['reads'], entry['p'] = pair['reads'], pair['probabilities']\n    49\t            if 'sign' in pair:\n    50\t                entry['sign'], entry['sp'] = pair['sign'], pair['probabilities']\n    51\t    return out\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef linked(entry, new, thesis):\n    55\t    \"\"\"(direction '<reader> reads <read>', sign) the product writes, or (None, None).\"\"\"\n    56\t    if entry['reads'] not in READS or entry['p'][entry['reads']] < THRESHOLD:\n    57\t        return None, None\n    58\t    if entry['sign'] not in SIGNS or entry['sp'][entry['sign']] < THRESHOLD:\n    59\t        return None, None\n    60\t    direction = f'{new} reads {thesis}' if entry['reads'] == 'candidate_reads_thesis' else f'{thesis} reads {new}'\n    61\t    return direction, entry['sign']\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef margin(entry):\n    65\t    values = sorted(entry['p'].values(), reverse=True)\n    66\t    return round(values[0] - values[1], 2)\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef score(draws, expected):\n    70\t    \"\"\"draws: [(name, decisions)]. Returns (rows, summary); refuses when a registered pair has no READS answer in a draw.\"\"\"\n    71\t    rows, wrong, missed, right, fragile, positive = [], [], [], [], [], []\n    72\t    for key, reg in expected.items():\n    73\t        seq, thesis = int(key.split(':')[0]), key.split(':')[1]\n    74\t        cells = []\n    75\t        for name, answers in draws:\n    76\t            entry = answers.get((seq, thesis))\n    77\t            if entry is None or entry['p'] is None:\n    78\t                raise Refused(f'{name}: no READS answer for the registered pair {key}')\n    79\t            direction, sign = linked(entry, reg['new'], thesis)\n    80\t            m = margin(entry)\n    81\t            short = {'candidate_reads_thesis': 'new→', 'thesis_reads_candidate': '←new', 'neither': 'none'}[entry['reads']]\n    82\t            cell = f\"{short} {entry['p'][entry['reads']]:.2f} (m {m:.2f})\" + (f\"; {entry['sign']} {entry['sp'][entry['sign']]:.2f}\" if entry['sign'] else '')\n    83\t            if reg['class'] == 'R':\n    84\t                if direction is None:\n    85\t                    verdict = 'missed'\n    86\t                elif direction == reg['direction'] and sign == REQUIRED_SIGN:\n    87\t                    verdict = 'right'\n    88\t                else:\n    89\t                    verdict = 'WRONG'\n    90\t                positive.append(verdict == 'right')\n    91\t            elif reg['class'] == 'W':\n    92\t                verdict = 'WRONG' if direction else 'right'\n    93\t            elif reg['class'] == 'F':\n    94\t                verdict = 'WRONG' if (direction, sign) == tuple(reg['forbidden']) else (f'linked: {direction} ({sign})' if direction else 'no link')\n    95\t            else:\n    96\t                verdict = f'linked: {direction} ({sign})' if direction else 'no link'\n    97\t            if verdict == 'WRONG':\n    98\t                wrong.append((name, key, direction, sign))\n    99\t            elif verdict == 'missed':\n   100\t                missed.append((name, key))\n   101\t            elif verdict == 'right' and reg['class'] == 'R':\n   102\t                right.append((name, key))\n   103\t            if (direction or reg['class'] == 'R') and m < 0.10:\n   104\t                fragile.append((name, key, m))\n   105\t            cells.append(f'{cell} → {verdict}')\n   106\t        rows.append((seq, reg, thesis, cells))\n   107\t    gate = not wrong and bool(positive) and all(positive)\n   108\t    return rows, {'right': right, 'missed': missed, 'wrong': wrong, 'fragile': fragile, 'gate': gate}\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef counted_draws(folders, wording=None):\n   112\t    if len(folders) != 3:\n   113\t        raise Refused(f'three census draws are required, got {len(folders)}')\n   114\t    seen = []\n   115\t    for folder in folders:\n   116\t        record_path = Path(folder) / 'draw.json'\n   117\t        if not record_path.exists():\n   118\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: no draw.json (not a census draw)')\n   119\t        record = json.loads(record_path.read_text())\n   120\t        if record.get('transport') != 'paid':\n   121\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: not a paid draw (transport {record.get(\"transport\")!r})')\n   122\t        if record.get('wording') != wording:\n   123\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: wording {record.get(\"wording\")!r}, expected {wording!r}')\n   124\t        if not record.get('counted'):\n   125\t            raise Refused(f'{folder}: the draw was not counted: {record.get(\"problems\")}')\n   126\t        seen.append(record['draw'])\n   127\t    if sorted(seen) != ['1', '2', '3']:\n   128\t        raise Refused(f'the draws must be 1, 2 and 3, got {seen}')\n   129\t    return [(Path(f).name, decisions(Path(f) / 'views.sqlite')) for f in folders]\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\tdef main(folders):\n   133\t    wording = None\n   134\t    if folders and folders[0] == '--v2':\n   135\t        wording, folders = 'v2', folders[1:]\n   136\t    expected = json.loads((HERE / ('expected-links-v2.json' if wording == 'v2' else 'expected-links.json')).read_text())\n   137\t    draws = counted_draws(folders, wording)\n   138\t    rows, summary = score(draws, expected)\n   139\t    print('# Census of the link decisions over the window, scored against the registered reading\\n')\n   140\t    print('| seq | new | shown | class | registered | ' + ' | '.join(name for name, _ in draws) + ' |')\n   141\t    print('|---|---|---|---|---|' + '---|' * len(draws))\n   142\t    for seq, reg, thesis, cells in rows:\n   143\t        print(f\"| {seq} | {reg['new']} | {thesis} | {reg['class']} | {reg['direction'] or ''} | \" + ' | '.join(cells) + ' |')\n   144\t    print(f'\\nDraws: 3 (the seq-148 jobs of each answered by its paired July sample).')\n   145\t    print(f\"Known positive right: {len(summary['right'])}; missed: {len(summary['missed'])} {summary['missed']}\")\n   146\t    print(f\"Wrong links: {len(summary['wrong'])} {summary['wrong']}\")\n   147\t    print(f\"Fragile (margin below 0.10 on a linked or required pair): {len(summary['fragile'])} {summary['fragile']}\")\n   148\t    print(f\"\\nGate (no wrong link in any draw; the known positive right in every draw): {'PASS' if summary['gate'] else 'FAIL'}\")\n   149\t\n   150\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def budget_module|gev_est|jev_(estimate|cost)|64_000|def is_link_request' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py; rg -n 'def _jev|def reserve|def settle|def install_stop_gate|def claim_launcher' ../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py ../../../docs/research/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py; rg -n '321:v|1238:v(9|14)|148:v9' expected-links-v2.json; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3049,3074p'; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | sed -n '68,95p' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def budget_module|gev_est|jev_(estimate|cost)|64_000|def is_link_request' ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py; rg -n 'def _jev|def reserve|def settle|def install_stop_gate|def claim_launcher' ../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py ../../../docs/research/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py; rg -n '321:v|1238:v(9|14)|148:v9' expected-links-v2.json; nl -ba ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3049,3074p'; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | sed -n '68,95p' \"","aggregated_output":"51:def is_link_request(request):\n459:def budget_module():\n467:    original_jev_estimate = module.jev_estimate\n468:    module.jev_estimate = lambda request: max(original_jev_estimate(request),\n476:    ATTEMPTS x reported input tokens, never above `jev_estimate`. With every settlement at or below its reservation, and a reservation\n489:            ratio, key = settled / budget.jev_estimate(request), 'match (Jev)'\nrg: ../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: ../../../docs/research/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n38: \"148:v9\": {\n128: \"321:v14\": {\n138: \"321:v16\": {\n148: \"321:v9\": {\n158: \"321:v1\": {\n164: \"321:v8\": {\n174: \"321:v2\": {\n180: \"321:v15\": {\n492: \"1238:v14\": {\n510: \"1238:v9\": {\n  3049\t## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n  3050\t\n  3051\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\n  3052\t- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\n  3053\t- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\n  3054\t- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n  3055\t\n  3056\t## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\n  3057\t\n  3058\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\".\n  3059\t- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \"假的测量\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\n  3060\t- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\n  3061\t- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\n  3062\t\n  3063\t## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\n  3064\t\n  3065\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, after reading the two readers' reasoning on every disagreement (readers A and B differed on 3 of 23 questions by range or yes/no and on 12 of 20 direction labels; the system disagreed with the draft on the total revenue and Vera CPU questions in every draw): \"那就不要理A了；我们就go with B 好吧，定下尺子金表\".\n  3066\t- Fixed by that decision: the ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md` (unit: a gold question at the window end 2026-07-14; material: golden-v5's 309 items by sha; a numeric question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match; the two null baselines printed with every score); the question list and the must_open mapping as built (`questions-v1.json`, 22 seeds + the Ohio guarantee); the gold `gold-v1.json` = reader B's 23 answers verbatim (B: a fresh-context Claude reader, model-authored, 3 questions marked no material: CoWoS capacity, semiconductor growth, SK Telecom), sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2` in `gold-v1.sha256` and in `score_judgement.py`, which refuses any other. Reader A (Codex) stays beside it as the control record (`reader-A.json`, `reconcile-v1.md`): its distance from B is the stick's own noise. Claude's two proposals of the afternoon (a three-level score when readers split; toss-up questions excluded) were not adopted: one range per question, every question counts. From here D261 applies: nothing in the ruler or the gold changes; a defect is a dated record in `corrections-v1.json`.\n  3067\t- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \"no judgement\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\n  3068\t\n  3069\t## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\n  3070\t\n  3071\t- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \"wrong\" on some questions: \"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\n  3072\t- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\n  3073\t- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\n  3074\t\n    68\t\n    69\t## 2. The two questions\n    70\t\n    71\t```\n    72\tREADS (choice), state = CANDIDATE (candidate_state), per THESIS:\n    73\t instructions: \"Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    74\t \"candidate_reads_thesis\": \"the CANDIDATE should be judged with the THESIS's current conclusion in view, because the THESIS's answer bounds or drives the CANDIDATE's: a part read against its whole (one product line's sales against the company's total sales; one region's loan book against the bank's total loans), or a quantity read against another it depends on (a component supplier's revenue against its largest customer's capital spending; an airline's fuel bill against its fuel volume)\"\n    75\t \"thesis_reads_candidate\": \"the THESIS should be judged with the CANDIDATE's current conclusion in view, for the same reasons with the roles swapped\"\n    76\t \"neither\": \"neither answer bounds or drives the other: unrelated quantities (a retailer's gross margin and its store openings in another country), or the same quantity for the same period and scope; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\"\n    77\t\n    78\tSIGN, two builders with the same three classes; state = CANDIDATE (candidate_state), per pair:\n    79\t when the CANDIDATE reads the THESIS: \"If the THESIS's answer turned out higher, which way would that move the CANDIDATE's most likely answer? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    80\t when the THESIS reads the CANDIDATE: \"If the CANDIDATE's answer turned out higher, which way would that move the THESIS's most likely answer? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    81\t \"together\": \"a higher answer to the question read makes a higher answer to the question reading it more likely (a company's total sales and one product line's sales, when that line's share of the total holds steady; a customer's capital spending and its component supplier's revenue)\"\n    82\t \"opposite\": \"a higher answer to the question read makes a lower answer to the question reading it more likely (an airline's fuel bill and its operating margin; a retailer's markdowns and its gross margin)\"\n    83\t \"no_clear_sign\": \"the question read only caps the other without moving its most likely answer (a regulator's cap on a bank's fees set far above what it charges), or the supplied text does not show which way it moves it\"\n    84\t```\n    85\t\n    86\tSources: PRD 06 (\"B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion\"; a numeric thesis reading another numeric thesis), D51 (chosen in the\n    87\tmatching step), D537 and council R (a part reads its whole), judging-v7 lines 4 and 9 (\"a part cannot exceed its whole\"; \"consistent\n    88\twith the conclusions of the theses it depends on\"). Every class has an example from another industry (retail, banking, airlines,\n    89\tcomponents), all number questions of the kind D695 admits; none names a company. Same-quantity-same-period is excluded because such a pair is one question (D248); another period of the\n    90\tsame quantity may be linked. A link with no sign is not written: the existing label vocabulary cannot express it (council R round 2).\n    91\t\n    92\t**Decision rule (code):** Jev's returned `choice` decides, accepted only when its probability is at least 0.5 (`THRESHOLD`, as every Jev\n    93\tanswer in `jev_matching` is read). Stage 1 `neither` or below 0.5: no link. Stage 2 `no_clear_sign` or below 0.5: no link. Every\n    94\toutcome is in the selection record.\n    95\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
