{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/links.py | sed -n '178,287p'; rg -n 'jev-wire|def jev_estimate|JEV_REQUEST_TOKENS|0.042' ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py ../../../src/hivemind/model.py; nl -ba CENSUS-RESULT.md | sed -n '1,44p'\"","aggregated_output":"   178\tdef _ask(archive, cfg, jobs, transport, record, stage):\n   179\t    \"\"\"One Jev request per job, asked in order; each job is written into the record before it is sent (its request sha, whether the\n   180\t    archive held it) and completed as it is answered (its call id). A failure names the failing job's sha and leaves the later jobs\n   181\t    marked not asked.\"\"\"\n   182\t    entries = []\n   183\t    for state, questions in jobs:\n   184\t        _, sha = model.request_identity(jev.request_for(cfg.matching, state, questions))\n   185\t        entries.append({'stage': stage, 'request_sha256': sha, 'questions': sorted(questions), 'archived_before': bool(archive.lookup(sha)),\n   186\t                        'status': 'not asked'})\n   187\t    record['calls'].extend(entries)\n   188\t    replies = []\n   189\t    for entry, (state, questions) in zip(entries, jobs):\n   190\t        try:\n   191\t            reply = jev.ask(archive, cfg, cfg.matching, state, questions, 'match', transport=transport)\n   192\t        except Exception as error:\n   193\t            entry['status'] = 'failed'\n   194\t            record['error'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:300]\n   195\t            record['failed_request_sha256'] = entry['request_sha256']\n   196\t            raise Refused(f'link question failed: {record[\"error\"]}', record) from error\n   197\t        entry['status'], entry['call_id'] = 'answered', reply.call_id\n   198\t        replies.append(reply.data)\n   199\t    return replies\n   200\t\n   201\t\n   202\tdef _passes(answer, accepted):\n   203\t    choice = answer['choice']\n   204\t    return choice if choice in accepted and answer['probabilities'][choice] >= THRESHOLD else None\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\tdef choose(archive, cfg, conn, handover, checked, lists, shown_views, *, transport=None):\n   208\t    \"\"\"The links this article proposes: [{'reader', 'read', 'candidate', 'direction', 'sign'}], reader and read being a candidate id\n   209\t    (canonical) or a stored view id; and the record of how they were chosen. Raises Refused for an unbound waiting row, a Jev\n   210\t    failure or a circle that remains after one correction (PRD 06).\"\"\"\n   211\t    record = {'pairs': [], 'calls': [], 'corrections': [], 'proposed': []}\n   212\t    if unbound_waits(conn):\n   213\t        record['error'] = 'the store holds an unbound waiting dependency row'\n   214\t        raise Refused(record['error'], record)\n   215\t    aliases, problems = identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates, checked.outcomes)\n   216\t    if problems:                                   # the writer refuses the same plan (WriteConflict); nothing to ask\n   217\t        record['skipped'] = problems\n   218\t        return [], record\n   219\t    evidence = handover.evidence\n   220\t    stage1, asked = [], []\n   221\t    for c in handover.candidates:\n   222\t        outcome, target, _ = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   223\t        if outcome not in ('new', 'succession') or aliases.get(c['id']) != c['id']:\n   224\t            continue\n   225\t        rungs = candidate_rungs(conn, c, outcome, target)\n   226\t        if not is_number_question(c['kind'], rungs, c.get('measure')):\n   227\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'eligible': False, 'why': 'not a number question'})\n   228\t            continue\n   229\t        listed = list(dict.fromkeys(list(lists.candidate_lists.get(c['id'], [])) + [v['view_id'] for v in shown_views]))\n   230\t        theses = []\n   231\t        for view_id in listed:\n   232\t            ok = store.is_open(conn, view_id) and stored_is_number_question(conn, view_id)\n   233\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'eligible': ok})\n   234\t            if ok:\n   235\t                theses.append(view_id)\n   236\t        if theses:\n   237\t            state = jev_matching.candidate_state(c, evidence)\n   238\t            stage1.append((state, {f'reads__{v}': reads_question(jev_matching.thesis_text(conn, v)) for v in theses}))\n   239\t            asked.append((c, state, theses))\n   240\t    if not stage1:\n   241\t        return [], record\n   242\t    answers = _ask(archive, cfg, stage1, transport, record, 'reads')\n   243\t    directions = {}\n   244\t    for (c, state, theses), reply in zip(asked, answers):\n   245\t        for view_id in theses:\n   246\t            answer = reply[f'reads__{view_id}']\n   247\t            direction = _passes(answer, (CANDIDATE_READS, THESIS_READS))\n   248\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'reads': answer['choice'], 'probabilities': answer['probabilities']})\n   249\t            if direction:\n   250\t                directions[(c['id'], view_id)] = direction\n   251\t    links = _signed(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, transport, record)\n   252\t    on_circle = circles(conn, links)\n   253\t    if on_circle:\n   254\t        links = _corrected(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, links, on_circle, transport, record)\n   255\t        remaining = circles(conn, links)\n   256\t        if remaining:\n   257\t            record['error'] = 'persistent cycle: ' + '; '.join(' -> '.join(path) for _, path in remaining)\n   258\t            raise Refused(record['error'], record)\n   259\t    record['proposed'] = links\n   260\t    return links, record\n   261\t\n   262\t\n   263\tdef _signed(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, transport, record, stage='sign'):\n   264\t    jobs, owners = [], []\n   265\t    for c, state, theses in asked:\n   266\t        questions = {f'sign__{v}': sign_question(jev_matching.thesis_text(conn, v), directions[(c['id'], v)]) for v in theses if (c['id'], v) in directions}\n   267\t        if questions:\n   268\t            jobs.append((state, questions))\n   269\t            owners.append(c)\n   270\t    links = []\n   271\t    if not jobs:\n   272\t        return links\n   273\t    for c, reply in zip(owners, _ask(archive, cfg, jobs, transport, record, stage)):\n   274\t        for qid, answer in sorted(reply.items()):\n   275\t            view_id = qid[len('sign__'):]\n   276\t            sign = _passes(answer, (TOGETHER, OPPOSITE))\n   277\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'sign': answer['choice'], 'probabilities': answer['probabilities']})\n   278\t            if sign:\n   279\t                direction = directions[(c['id'], view_id)]\n   280\t                reader, read = (c['id'], view_id) if direction == CANDIDATE_READS else (view_id, c['id'])\n   281\t                links.append({'reader': reader, 'read': read, 'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'direction': direction, 'sign': sign})\n   282\t    return links\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\tdef _corrected(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, links, on_circle, transport, record):\n   286\t    \"\"\"PRD 06: refuse a circle and ask the model to correct it, once: the pair's READS question again, the offending direction removed\n   287\t    and the circle named; the answer replaces the original.\"\"\"\n../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:435:JEV_REQUEST_TOKENS = 64000       # TypeSafe's published default per-request limit (docs.typesafe.ai/models, context length), council R round 11\n../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:469:                                              module.jev.ATTEMPTS * JEV_REQUEST_TOKENS * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6)\n../../../src/hivemind/model.py:36:          'jev-1.14.0': (0.042, 0.0)}   # Jev: docs.typesafe.ai/models, 2026-10-25; output free   # DeepSeek: peak-hour list prices, cache misses (2026-10-23 pricing page)\n../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:256:def jev_estimate(request):\n     1\t# The census of link decisions over the window: gate PASS by the registered rule; direction unsettled (D700, D701; 2026-11-21)\n     2\t\n     3\tRun: `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/` (three draws, each counted: complete, both July seq-148 answers reused, equal to old-2 with no\n     4\tlink row; one ledger at Alex's $0.10: settled $0.0266 at the ledger's rule of three times each reported input, 52 attempts, nothing\n     5\trefused or overrun). Scored by `read_census.py` against `expected-links.json` (written before any census answer; R 1, W 38, O 66):\n     6\t`census-pairs.md` (every pair and draw).\n     7\t\n     8\t## By the registered rule\n     9\t- **Known positive (v9 Data Center FY2027 reads v14 total revenue FY2027, together):** right in 3 of 3 draws; margins 0.05, 0.09,\n    10\t  0.03 (the July samples, fragile).\n    11\t- **W pairs (38, the shown material names no connection):** no link in any draw. Wrong links: 0.\n    12\t- **Gate: PASS.**\n    13\t\n    14\t## The O pairs that were linked (reported, not scored)\n    15\t\n    16\t| seq | pair | draw 1 | draw 2 | draw 3 | reading |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| 8 | v2 (all credit support, guarantees, backstops) – v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | v2 reads v1, 0.58 | v2 reads v1, 0.51 | no link (0.48) | a whole reads its part; 2 of 3 |\n    19\t| 265 | v16 (total CPU FY2027) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v16 reads v14, 0.82 | 0.82 | 0.83 | a part reads its whole; stable |\n    20\t| 321 | v17 (total revenue growth FY2028) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v17 reads v16, 0.50 | 0.50 | 0.55 | a company-wide figure reads a part of the year before; at the line |\n    21\t| 534 | v21 (total revenue growth FY2027) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v21 reads v16, 0.73 | 0.72 | 0.76 | a whole reads its part; stable |\n    22\t| 534 | v21 – v9 (Data Center FY2027) | v21 reads v9, 0.53 | **v9 reads v21**, 0.52 | v21 reads v9, 0.60 | the direction flips between draws |\n    23\t| 1238 | v35 (total revenue FY2028) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v35 reads v14, 0.52 | 0.54 | no link (0.44) | another period of the same quantity; 2 of 3 |\n    24\t| 1238 | v35 – v9 | no link | v35 reads v9, 0.50 | no link | 1 of 3 |\n    25\t\n    26\tEvery proposed link carried the sign together. Proposals per draw: 7, 8, 5 (proposals: the census writes no link).\n    27\t\n    28\t## What it shows\n    29\t- **No link between unrelated questions.** Across 3 × 38 W decisions, Jev never linked a financing amount to a revenue or margin\n    30\t  question, or two financing amounts of different kinds.\n    31\t- **The direction of a part against its whole is not settled by the criterion.** The same version reads part-to-whole (v9 → v14,\n    32\t  v16 → v14) and whole-to-part (v2 → v1, v21 → v16, v21 → v9), and one pair flips between draws (v21–v9). This is the class §3 named\n    33\t  (\"abstract\": the criterion's two clauses admit both directions), now counted on the whole window: of the 8 pairs linked in some draw,\n    34\t  4 take the same direction in 3 of 3 draws (v9 → v14, v16 → v14, v17 → v16, v21 → v16), 3 are linked in only 1 or 2 draws, and 1\n    35\t  flips direction.\n    36\t- **Fragile decisions:** 6 of the linked or required decisions sit within 0.10 of the next class (v9 → v14 in all three; v17 → v16 in\n    37\t  two; v21–v9 in one).\n    38\t\n    39\t## What it means for the paid run\n    40\t- A linked sequence of the paid run can take its link answers from its paired census draw: a link request depends on the candidate's\n    41\t  state and the shown question's card, ladder and first two evidence pieces, none of which a written link changes, so the requests are\n    42\t  the same (a circle correction, if any, would be new). The readers are then known before anything is bought: draw 1 and draw 2, v2,\n    43\t  v9, v16, v17, v21, v35; draw 3, v9, v16, v17, v21. Each control can retire exactly its paired draw's readers from each reader's first\n    44\t  link.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3, json, pathlib, collections, sys\nw=next(pathlib.Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/window/probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite'\\\\''))\nc=sqlite3.connect(w.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nd=sqlite3.connect(w.with_name('\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nt=0; reserve=[]; nquestions=0\nfor seq,record in d.execute(\\\"select seq, record_json from link_selections where status='\\\\''proposed'\\\\''\\\"):\n for call in json.loads(record).get('\\\\''calls'\\\\'',[]):\n  cid,raw=c.execute('\\\\''select call_id, request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?'\\\\'',(call['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n  r=json.loads(raw); qs=r['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']; state=r['\\\\''state'\\\\'']\n  n=len(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False).encode('\\\\''utf8'\\\\''))\n  t+=n\n  reserve.append(max(64000, n*2+4096)*3*0.042/1e6)\n  nquestions+=len(qs)\n  if seq not in (148,321,1238) or call['\\\\''stage'\\\\''] \"'!= '\"'\\\\''reads'\\\\'': continue\n  print(seq,cid,state)\n  for name,q in qs.items():\n   if name in ('\\\\''reads__v14'\\\\'','\\\\''reads__v9'\\\\'','\\\\''reads__v16'\\\\'','\\\\''reads__v8'\\\\''):\n    print(name,q['\\\\''instructions'\\\\''])\nprint('\\\\''jobs'\\\\'',len(reserve),'\\\\''bytes'\\\\'',t,'\\\\''max reservation'\\\\'',max(reserve),'\\\\''questions'\\\\'',nquestions,'\\\\''estimate at 0.37 bytes'\\\\'',t*0.37*3*0.042/1e6)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3, json, pathlib, collections, sys\nw=next(pathlib.Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/window/probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite'\\\\''))\nc=sqlite3.connect(w.as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nd=sqlite3.connect(w.with_name('\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nt=0; reserve=[]; nquestions=0\nfor seq,record in d.execute(\\\"select seq, record_json from link_selections where status='\\\\''proposed'\\\\''\\\"):\n for call in json.loads(record).get('\\\\''calls'\\\\'',[]):\n  cid,raw=c.execute('\\\\''select call_id, request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?'\\\\'',(call['\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\''],)).fetchone()\n  r=json.loads(raw); qs=r['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']; state=r['\\\\''state'\\\\'']\n  n=len(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False).encode('\\\\''utf8'\\\\''))\n  t+=n\n  reserve.append(max(64000, n*2+4096)*3*0.042/1e6)\n  nquestions+=len(qs)\n  if seq not in (148,321,1238) or call['\\\\''stage'\\\\''] \"'!= '\"'\\\\''reads'\\\\'': continue\n  print(seq,cid,state)\n  for name,q in qs.items():\n   if name in ('\\\\''reads__v14'\\\\'','\\\\''reads__v9'\\\\'','\\\\''reads__v16'\\\\'','\\\\''reads__v8'\\\\''):\n    print(name,q['\\\\''instructions'\\\\''])\nprint('\\\\''jobs'\\\\'',len(reserve),'\\\\''bytes'\\\\'',t,'\\\\''max reservation'\\\\'',max(reserve),'\\\\''questions'\\\\'',nquestions,'\\\\''estimate at 0.37 bytes'\\\\'',t*0.37*3*0.042/1e6)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"148 8744 CANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nKey: measure=total_revenue, period_start=2026-02-01, period_end=2027-01-31, unit=USD\nLadder: Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $450 billion. / Bullish: Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. / Neutral: Total revenue is at least $350 billion but less than $400 billion. / Bearish: Total revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $350 billion. / Strongly bearish: Total revenue is less than $300 billion.\nIts evidence: [Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg ] The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\nreads__v8 Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\nv8 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA stand-alone CPU sales\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?\n    Ladder: Strongly bullish: Stand-alone CPU sales exceed $25 billion in FY2027. / Bullish: Stand-alone CPU sales are at least $20 billion and no more than $25 billion in FY2027. / Neutral: Stand-alone CPU sales are at least $15 billion and less than $20 billion in FY2027. / Bearish: Stand-alone CPU sales are at least $10 billion and less than $15 billion in FY2027. / Strongly bearish: Stand-alone CPU sales are less than $10 billion in FY2027.\n    Evidence: [fool.com (analyst) ] Intel has led here for years and holds more than 59% of total CPU market share\n    Evidence: [fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-05] AMD has gained ground, progressing from a low of about 17% back in 2016 to 38% today.\nreads__v9 Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\nv9 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Ladder: Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $450 billion. / Bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion. / Neutral: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion. / Bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion. / Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is below $300 billion.\n    Evidence: [tradingview.com ] During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\n    Evidence: [NVIDIA 2026-07-07] NVIDIA is collaborating with Nokia to deliver AI-RAN platforms integrated with Nokia anyRAN software for AI-native 5G-Advanced networks ready for 6G evolution.\n321 8751 CANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA FY2028 total revenue growth\", FY2028, due 2028-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2028?\nKey: measure=growth_rate, scope=total revenue, period_start=2027-02-01, period_end=2028-01-31, unit=percent\nLadder: Strongly bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 60%. / Bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 50% but less than 60%. / Neutral: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 35% but less than 50%. / Bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 20% but less than 35%. / Strongly bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is less than 20%.\nIts evidence: [fool.com (analyst) ] they also predict growth slowing to a 41% revenue increase for fiscal 2028.\nreads__v14 Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\nv14 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Ladder: Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $450 billion. / Bullish: Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. / Ne