('\\\\''retained v35 reads v9'\\\\'',score.linked(table[1238,'\\\\''v9'\\\\''],'\\\\''v35'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\''))\n a=table[321,'\\\\''v16'\\\\'']; a.update(reads='\\\\''neither'\\\\'',p={'\\\\''neither'\\\\'':1,'\\\\''candidate_reads_thesis'\\\\'':0,'\\\\''thesis_reads_candidate'\\\\'':0},sign=None,sp=None)\n draws.append((str(n),table))\nprint('\\\\''mutant preserving both other defects'\\\\'',score.score(draws,v2)[1])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"draw 1 jobs 20 actual incl July 0.009479231999999999\nestimate v2 incl July using original shape + growth 0.01151083836\ndraw 2 jobs 20 actual incl July 0.009479231999999999\nestimate v2 incl July using original shape + growth 0.01151083836\ndraw 3 jobs 18 actual incl July 0.009111942\nestimate v2 incl July using original shape + growth 0.01112718474\nclasses Counter({'O': 62, 'W': 38, 'F': 4, 'R': 1})\nretained v35 reads v9 ('v35 reads v9', 'together')\nmutant preserving both other defects {'right': [('1', '148:v9'), ('2', '148:v9'), ('3', '148:v9')], 'missed': [], 'wrong': [], 'fragile': [('1', '148:v9', 0.05), ('2', '148:v9', 0.09), ('3', '148:v9', 0.03), ('2', '534:v9', 0.09)], 'gate': True}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '345,368p'; rg -n '\"'^(INFO|'\"\\\\S).*config' preflight-window.log | head; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/links.py | sed -n '285,322p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '345,368p'; rg -n '\"'^(INFO|'\"\\\\S).*config' preflight-window.log | head; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/links.py | sed -n '285,322p'\"","aggregated_output":"   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   285\tdef _corrected(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, links, on_circle, transport, record):\n   286\t    \"\"\"PRD 06: refuse a circle and ask the model to correct it, once: the pair's READS question again, the offending direction removed\n   287\t    and the circle named; the answer replaces the original.\"\"\"\n   288\t    offending = {(link['candidate'], link['thesis']): path for link, path in on_circle}\n   289\t    jobs, owners = [], []\n   290\t    for c, state, theses in asked:\n   291\t        questions = {}\n   292\t        for view_id in theses:\n   293\t            path = offending.get((c['id'], view_id))\n   294\t            if path is None:\n   295\t                continue\n   296\t            excluded = directions[(c['id'], view_id)]\n   297\t            named = [('the CANDIDATE' if node == c['id'] else 'the THESIS' if node == view_id else node) for node in path]\n   298\t            note = f'Reading this way would make {named[0]} read itself through {\" -> \".join(named)}; a question cannot read its own conclusion.'\n   299\t            questions[f'reads__{view_id}'] = reads_question(jev_matching.thesis_text(conn, view_id), excluded=excluded, note=note)\n   300\t            record['corrections'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'rejected': excluded, 'path': path})\n   301\t        if questions:\n   302\t            jobs.append((state, questions))\n   303\t            owners.append(c)\n   304\t    kept = [link for link in links if (link['candidate'], link['thesis']) not in offending]\n   305\t    corrected = {}\n   306\t    for c, reply in zip(owners, _ask(archive, cfg, jobs, transport, record, 'correction')):\n   307\t        for qid, answer in reply.items():\n   308\t            view_id = qid[len('reads__'):]\n   309\t            directions.pop((c['id'], view_id), None)\n   310\t            direction = _passes(answer, (CANDIDATE_READS, THESIS_READS))\n   311\t            record['corrections'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'answer': answer['choice'], 'probabilities': answer['probabilities']})\n   312\t            if direction:\n   313\t                corrected[(c['id'], view_id)] = direction\n   314\t    if corrected:\n   315\t        directions.update(corrected)\n   316\t        regrouped = [(c, state, [v for v in theses if (c['id'], v) in corrected]) for c, state, theses in asked]\n   317\t        kept += _signed(archive, cfg, conn, [g for g in regrouped if g[2]], corrected, transport, record, stage='correction sign')\n   318\t    return kept\n   319\t\n   320\t\n   321\t# ---------- the record ----------\n   322\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,sqlite3\nd=next(pathlib.Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/window/probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite'\\\\'')).parent\na=sqlite3.connect((d/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nv=sqlite3.connect((d/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\ncalls=[]\nfor seq, rec in v.execute(\\\"select seq,record_json from link_selections where status='\\\\''proposed'\\\\'' order by id\\\"):\n for call in json.loads(rec)['\\\\''calls'\\\\'']:\n  raw=a.execute('\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()[0]\n  req=json.loads(raw)\n  size=len(json.dumps(req,sort_keys=True,ensure_ascii=False).encode('\\\\''utf-8'\\\\''))\n  reserve=max(64000,2*size+4096)*0.000000126\n  calls.append((seq,call['\\\\''stage'\\\\''],len(req['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']),size,reserve,call['\\\\''archived_before'\\\\'']))\nprint('\\\\''count'\\\\'',len(calls),'\\\\''read/sign split'\\\\'',collections.Counter(c[1] for c in calls),'\\\\''lookups before'\\\\'',sum(c[-1] for c in calls))\nprint('\\\\''biggest'\\\\'',max(calls,key=lambda x:x[4]))\ns=0; remaining=0.1-0.02655387\nfor i, (seq,stage,_,size,rv,_) in enumerate(calls*3,1):\n if s+rv > remaining:\n  print('\\\\''stress first refusal'\\\\'',i,seq,stage,'\\\\''spend'\\\\'',s,'\\\\''reserve'\\\\'',rv); break\n s += size*0.37*0.000000126\nprint('\\\\''total stress'\\\\'',sum(x[3] for x in calls)*3*0.37*0.000000126)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import collections,json,pathlib,sqlite3\nd=next(pathlib.Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/window/probe-v2-dry/archive.sqlite'\\\\'')).parent\na=sqlite3.connect((d/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\nv=sqlite3.connect((d/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'').as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\ncalls=[]\nfor seq, rec in v.execute(\\\"select seq,record_json from link_selections where status='\\\\''proposed'\\\\'' order by id\\\"):\n for call in json.loads(rec)['\\\\''calls'\\\\'']:\n  raw=a.execute('\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\'',(call['\\\\''call_id'\\\\''],)).fetchone()[0]\n  req=json.loads(raw)\n  size=len(json.dumps(req,sort_keys=True,ensure_ascii=False).encode('\\\\''utf-8'\\\\''))\n  reserve=max(64000,2*size+4096)*0.000000126\n  calls.append((seq,call['\\\\''stage'\\\\''],len(req['\\\\''questions'\\\\'']),size,reserve,call['\\\\''archived_before'\\\\'']))\nprint('\\\\''count'\\\\'',len(calls),'\\\\''read/sign split'\\\\'',collections.Counter(c[1] for c in calls),'\\\\''lookups before'\\\\'',sum(c[-1] for c in calls))\nprint('\\\\''biggest'\\\\'',max(calls,key=lambda x:x[4]))\ns=0; remaining=0.1-0.02655387\nfor i, (seq,stage,_,size,rv,_) in enumerate(calls*3,1):\n if s+rv > remaining:\n  print('\\\\''stress first refusal'\\\\'',i,seq,stage,'\\\\''spend'\\\\'',s,'\\\\''reserve'\\\\'',rv); break\n s += size*0.37*0.000000126\nprint('\\\\''total stress'\\\\'',sum(x[3] for x in calls)*3*0.37*0.000000126)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"count 28 read/sign split Counter({'reads': 14, 'sign': 14}) lookups before 0\nbiggest (1262, 'reads', 14, 36844, 0.009800784, False)\nstress first refusal 79 1102 reads spend 0.0653188158 reserve 0.008563715999999999\ntotal stress 0.07410356225999999\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The wording points toward the right July link, but the gate can pass while retaining one of the unsupported cross-period links this probe is meant to remove. I reproduced that false pass using the stored census answers. [Probe objective](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:36) · [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:83)\n\n### 1. Prompt audit\n\n- **Tie-break.** D537 supports letting the question with the weaker anchor read the better-anchored question when the relationship works both ways. D260 explains why consensus, guidance and reported figures matter. The general tie-break is a proposal authorized for this probe by D703. D537 decided the concrete Data Center case, and D260 governs judging. The audit should make that distinction explicit. [D537](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6457) · [D260](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3053) · [D703](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10556)\n- **Periods clause.** The older design permits links across periods. Requiring a mechanism in the supplied text is the proposed narrowing under D703. The generic retailer example is industry-neutral, but it needs to say that the text **merely names** this year's sales and next year's growth. Otherwise it looks like a blanket rejection of the same quantities the new SIGN example calls opposite. [Original design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:86) · [Revised examples](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:20)\n- **Base-effect example.** The arithmetic is correct with the next-year level held fixed. It fits the existing SIGN questions, which ask what happens when the read quantity rises. It also fits `no_clear_sign` when the supplied facts leave the effect unclear. Both new examples are generic and use no covered company, product, figure or test-article detail. [SIGN criteria and instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:32) · [Version 2 text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:305)\n\n### 2. July direction\n\nI read the seq-148 request in the dry archive, call **8744**. The total-revenue candidate has Bloomberg's **$393B FY2027** estimate. Data Center has **$75.25B for Q1**, 92% of company sales that quarter, and an AI-RAN announcement. The total has a direct full-year anchor and the segment has a partial-year observation. Read that way, the tie-break gives **v9 reads v14**. I would make “for its period” explicit as “for the quantity and full period the question asks about,” so a reported quarter cannot be mistaken for a full-year anchor. The reversed class applies the same test with the roles swapped, so a whole can still read a better-anchored part when either direction would help. [Request inputs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Reversed criterion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:28) · [Tie-break](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:305)\n\n### 3. Cross-period cases\n\nI read the seq-321 and seq-1238 requests in the dry archive, calls **8751** and **8763**.\n\n| Link | What the supplied text supports |\n|---|---|\n| `v17 reads v16` | The FY2027 CPU estimate and FY2028 company growth forecast supply no bridge from CPU sales to the next year's growth. Reject at READS. Flipping the sign alone leaves that gap. |\n| `v35 reads v9` | The prior-year Data Center quarter and next-year company forecast supply no segment carry-forward. Reject at READS. |\n| `v35 reads v14` | The candidate gives consecutive years' company totals and an outlook that translates FY2028 growth into a revenue level. That supplies a bridge through the FY2027 company base. The clause should leave this link available. |\n\nThat is how the revised rule should read. The dry run establishes the request contents and replay behavior. It used fake answers, so the three fresh draws are what test whether Jev follows the rule. [Periods clause](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:307) · [Prior findings on the same pairs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/CENSUS-RESULT.md:52) · [Dry-run result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-dry.log:65)\n\n### 4. Registration, harness and budget\n\n- **Blocking — the gate misses the READS failure.** The four F entries are sound as a targeted test for the unsupported `together` sign. They allow `v17 reads v16, opposite`, and `1238:v9` remains O. I changed only the three stored `321:v16` choices to `neither` in memory. The scorer returned **PASS** while retaining `v35 reads v9, together` in draw 2. Before sending, register **any accepted link** on `321:v16` and `1238:v9` as a failure under the cross-period rule. Keep `1238:v14` open and report it explicitly. Add a $0 negative check for each forbidden link, including the opposite-sign CPU case. [F registration](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected_links.py:77) · [Data Center entry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected-links-v2.json:510) · [Gate logic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:91)\n- **Budget — enough on the observed shapes, completion uncertain.** The existing ledger has **$0.07344613** left. Repricing the three observed job shapes from stored usage, including fresh July jobs and estimated wording growth, gives **about $0.034** for all three draws. The all-SIGN dry shape at the design's stress ratio of 0.37 tokens per byte estimates **$0.0741** in settlements, with a largest single reservation of **$0.00980**. That shape can stop before draw 3 completes. The reservation check protects the approved ceiling. Record a ceiling stop as an incomplete probe with no verdict, and use the existing D700 ledger for all three sequential draws. [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json:2) · [Stress assumption](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:131) · [Reservation check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:131)\n- **Reporting fix.** The $0 replay completed all 28 jobs with zero link rows written, and the old-wording mutant stopped before transport. The scorer correctly refuses old-wording draws under `--v2`, but its output still says the July answers were reused. Make the report say that v2 asks those jobs fresh. [Dry replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-dry.log:12) · [Mutant](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/probe-v2-mutant.log:1) · [Scorer output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:144)\n\n### 5. Verdict\n\nClarify the full-period anchor and the cross-period example, then freeze the two missing READS checks and show each rejects its stored counterexample at $0. Correct the July report and document the incomplete-probe outcome under the existing cap. No paid calls were made in this review.\n\n**NOT READY**"}}
